Third-party material
--------------------

No third-party code, data, artwork or fonts are embedded in the RescueForge
source tree. The icon is drawn by build.rs. All file system readers, format
readers and test-image builders were written for this project from the
publicly documented layouts of the formats.

Rust crates
  RescueForge is built with open-source Rust crates, among them eframe / egui,
  image (with its PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, WebP and TIFF codecs), miniz_oxide,
  serde, serde_json, rfd, tiny-skia, embed-resource and the windows crate.
  Each is used under its own licence (MIT and/or Apache-2.0 for most; zlib for
  some); see Cargo.lock for the exact versions and each crate for its terms.
  Their compiled code is part of RescueForge.exe.

Fonts
  RescueForge loads the Segoe UI and Segoe MDL2 Assets fonts that are installed
  with Windows at run time. They are not distributed with RescueForge. The
  default fonts bundled with egui (Ubuntu-Light, Hack, Noto Emoji and
  emoji-icon-font) are compiled in as fallbacks under their own licences
  (Ubuntu Font Licence, MIT, OFL), as listed by the egui project.
